.TH SOJU-TUI 1 "2026-08-27" "soju-tui" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soju-tui \- terminal administration frontend for the soju IRC bouncer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soju-tui
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soju-tui
is an interactive, administration-only terminal frontend for soju. It invokes
.B sojuctl
through the configured administrative Unix socket and does not run as a daemon.
.PP
The local account running the command must already have access to Soju's
administrative socket. Debian and Ubuntu package users can explicitly run
.BR soju-tui-setup (8)
as an administrator to configure that access on a systemd host.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Use the specified Soju configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-sojuctl " path"
Use the specified sojuctl executable.
.TP
.BI \-profile " path"
Use the specified local administrator profile.
.TP
.BI \-timeout " duration"
Set the maximum duration of an individual sojuctl operation.
.TP
.BI \-soju-systemd-unit " unit"
Select the optional Soju unit used for uptime and connection-age inspection.
An empty value disables this enrichment.
.TP
.B \-setup
Rediscover and recreate the local administrator profile. This does not grant
socket access or install system files.
.TP
.B \-accept-config
Accept discovered first-run settings without an interactive confirmation.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and source revision, then exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/soju/config
Default Soju configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/soju-tui/admin.json
Default mode-0600 local profile containing non-secret paths.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sojuctl (1),
.BR soju (1),
.BR soju-tui-setup (8)
.SH AUTHOR
The soju-tui contributors.
